  id: S01_04
  era: "c. 40,000 yrs ago \xB7 Section 1 \xB7 Prehistoric India \xB7 c. 1.5 million years ago \u2013 700 BCE"
  title: Upper Palaeolithic
  text: The Upper Palaeolithic, from about 40,000 years ago, brought long, thin stone blades, burins, bone tools and the first ornaments, such as ostrich-eggshell beads. Modern humans, Homo sapiens, spread across the subcontinent. Patne in Maharashtra and the Belan valley are key sites.
